    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_10_positive_instruction_redesign_design_doctrine_composition_prohibitions_backfire",
      "label": "Doctrine Rule 4: Composition Prohibitions Backfire; Only a Positive Composition Recipe Moves Them",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "rationale": "When the model has its own agenda for the output (e.g. restating specs feels like helpful curation), a prohibition like \"don't restate the brief\" measurably backfired (4.4 re-typed spec values vs 3.6 with no guidance), while a positive recipe scored 3.0 with zero variance; appending nuance clauses to a winning recipe degrades it (3.8 noisy vs 3.0 consistent).",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\specs\\2026-06-10-positive-instruction-redesign-design.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
